<title>FRANCE: Algeria expects $11.1 bln from 1997 energy exports.</title>
<headline>Algeria expects $11.1 bln from 1997 energy exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC member Algeria expects to earn $11.1 billion from the sale in 1997 of hydrocarbons including gas and oil, the official news agency APS said.</p>
<p>In a roundup of the main figures in the budget being discussed for a second day on Thursday by the National Transitional Council, the agency said imports were expected to total $11.7 billion next year.</p>
<p>Energy income was based on an average price of $17.5 per barrel of oil, and the country expected an average exchange rate of $1 to 56 dinars.</p>
<p>Gross domestic product was expected to total 2,654 billion dinars, the agency said.</p>
</text>
